# Singapore succession — scenario cases

## Constructors

<!-- l4: decide:surviving -->

**1.** In relation to a STRING “n”, surviving means Person where name is n, survived the deceased is TRUE and issue is EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:predeceased -->

**2.** In relation to a STRING “n” and a list of Person “kids”, predeceased means Person where name is n, survived the deceased is FALSE and issue is kids.

<!-- l4: decide:an intestate leaving -->

**3.** In relation to a list of Person “sp”, a list of Person “ch”, a list of Person “pa” and a list of Person “sb”, an intestate leaving means Case where deceased is Deceased where name is the deceased, date of death is YMD with 2026, 1 and 15, domiciled in Singapore is TRUE and Muslim is FALSE, family is Family where surviving spouses is sp, children is ch, parents is pa, siblings is sb, grandparents is EMPTY and uncles and aunts is EMPTY, estate is Estate where immovable property in Singapore is 900000, movable property in Singapore is 100000, funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is 0 and debts and liabilities is 0 and will is NOTHING.

## Reading a distribution

<!-- l4: decide:the total of -->

**4.** In relation to a list of Share “shares”, the total of means sum with map with given s then s's fraction and shares.

<!-- l4: decide:the share of -->

**5.** In relation to a STRING “who” and a list of Share “shares”, the share of means sum with map with given s then s's fraction and filter with given s then s's taker is equal to who and shares.

## 1. The ordinary scenarios

<!-- l4: decide:widow alone -->

**6.** Widow alone means an intestate leaving with list of surviving with Wife, EMPTY, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:widow and two children -->

**7.** Widow and two children means an intestate leaving with list of surviving with Wife, list of surviving with Ann and surviving with Ben, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:widow and two parents -->

**8.** Widow and two parents means an intestate leaving with list of surviving with Wife, EMPTY, list of surviving with Mum and surviving with Dad and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:three children -->

**9.** Three children means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, list of surviving with Ann, surviving with Ben and surviving with Cal, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:one child survives, one left grandchildren -->

**10.** One child survives, one left grandchildren means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, list of surviving with Ann and predeceased _ leaving _ with Ben and list of surviving with Gia and surviving with Gus, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:one child survives, one died childless -->

**11.** One child survives, one died childless means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, list of surviving with Ann and predeceased _ leaving _ with Ben and EMPTY, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:no relatives -->

**12.** No relatives means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:two siblings -->

**13.** Two siblings means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY and list of surviving with Sis and surviving with Bro.

## 2. Fork witnesses

<!-- l4: decide:all children predeceased, uneven stocks -->

**14.** All children predeceased, uneven stocks means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, list of predeceased _ leaving _ with Ann and list of surviving with Gia and surviving with Gus and predeceased _ leaving _ with Ben and list of surviving with Hal, EMPTY and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:F1 under R1 -->

**15.** F1 under R1 means the section 7 shares under _ of _ with the orthodox reading and all children predeceased, uneven stocks.

<!-- l4: decide:F1 under R2 -->

**16.** F1 under R2 means the section 7 shares under _ of _ with the per capita reading and all children predeceased, uneven stocks.

<!-- l4: decide:deceased sibling with deceased child -->

**17.** Deceased sibling with deceased child means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY and list of surviving with Sis and predeceased _ leaving _ with Bro and list of predeceased _ leaving _ with Nephew and list of surviving with Grandniece.

<!-- l4: decide:half blood and whole blood siblings -->

**18.** Half blood and whole blood siblings means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY and list of surviving with WholeBloodSis and surviving with HalfBloodBro.

<!-- l4: decide:foreign domicile, Singapore house only -->

**19.** Foreign domicile, Singapore house only means Case where deceased is Deceased where name is the deceased, date of death is YMD with 2026, 1 and 15, domiciled in Singapore is FALSE and Muslim is FALSE, family is Family where surviving spouses is list of surviving with Wife, children is EMPTY, parents is EMPTY, siblings is EMPTY, grandparents is EMPTY and uncles and aunts is EMPTY, estate is Estate where immovable property in Singapore is 900000, movable property in Singapore is 100000, funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is 0 and debts and liabilities is 0 and will is NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:child entered -->

**20.** Child entered means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, list of surviving with the child, EMPTY and list of surviving with Sis.

<!-- l4: decide:child not entered -->

**21.** Child not entered means an intestate leaving with EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY and list of surviving with Sis.

<!-- l4: decide:partial intestacy, half disposed -->

**22.** Partial intestacy, half disposed means Case where deceased is Deceased where name is the deceased, date of death is YMD with 2026, 1 and 15, domiciled in Singapore is TRUE and Muslim is FALSE, family is Family where surviving spouses is list of surviving with Wife, children is EMPTY, parents is EMPTY, siblings is EMPTY, grandparents is EMPTY and uncles and aunts is EMPTY, estate is Estate where immovable property in Singapore is 900000, movable property in Singapore is 100000, funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is 0 and debts and liabilities is 0 and will is JUST with Will where in writing is TRUE, signed at the foot or end by the testator is TRUE, number of attesting witnesses is 2, witnesses present at the same time is TRUE, witnesses subscribed in the testator's presence is TRUE, testator's age at execution is 55, soldier in actual military service or mariner at sea is FALSE, married after execution is FALSE, expressed to be made in contemplation of that marriage is FALSE, revoked by a later will, writing or destruction is FALSE, proportion of the estate beneficially disposed of is the result of dividing 1 by 2 and an executor is appointed, and able and willing to act is TRUE.

## 3. The Act's own boundaries

<!-- l4: decide:a Muslim intestate -->

**23.** A Muslim intestate means Case where deceased is Deceased where name is the deceased, date of death is YMD with 2026, 1 and 15, domiciled in Singapore is TRUE and Muslim is TRUE, family is Family where surviving spouses is list of surviving with Wife, children is EMPTY, parents is EMPTY, siblings is EMPTY, grandparents is EMPTY and uncles and aunts is EMPTY, estate is Estate where immovable property in Singapore is 900000, movable property in Singapore is 100000, funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is 0 and debts and liabilities is 0 and will is NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:a death in 1960 -->

**24.** A death in 1960 means Case where deceased is Deceased where name is the deceased, date of death is YMD with 1960, 5 and 1, domiciled in Singapore is TRUE and Muslim is FALSE, family is Family where surviving spouses is list of surviving with Wife, children is EMPTY, parents is EMPTY, siblings is EMPTY, grandparents is EMPTY and uncles and aunts is EMPTY, estate is Estate where immovable property in Singapore is 900000, movable property in Singapore is 100000, funeral, testamentary and administration expenses is 0 and debts and liabilities is 0 and will is NOTHING.

